<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman wars in Europe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century–<a href="/years/1923">1923</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> were a series of conflicts between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and European states from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-middle-ages">Late Middle Ages</a> to the early 20th century. After seizing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli</a> in 1354 the Ottomans expanded through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> and pushed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a> in the 15th and 16th centuries, while their wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> lasted from 1423 to 1718 and included their fleet's defeat at Lepanto in 1571. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1684">Holy League</a> reversed a number of Ottoman gains in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a> of 1683–99. The final retreat began with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a> of 1912–1913 and ended in the partitioning of the empire after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">World War I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-wars-in-europe.jpg" alt="Ottoman wars in Europe" width="330" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Geffels · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vienna_Battle_1683.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
